Attempt 1: read-only preflight SQL incorrectly placed the external `pg_isready` command inside SQL; PostgreSQL returned syntax error before any filesystem or database change. Corrected by running pg_isready as a separate shell command.
Attempt 2: attempted to write pg_dump output under /var/lib/riverview/backups/m4.1. Existing /var/lib/riverview mode 0700 is owned by riverview, so the postgres OS user could not traverse to the child directory. pg_dump failed before reading/writing the archive; no existing service data was modified. Kept the restrictive state-directory permissions and moved the backup to the postgres-owned, mode-0700 /var/lib/postgresql/backups tree.
